&lt;p&gt;Here are some available intern and graduate positions on offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Engineers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance next-generation semiconductor technology by running experiments, process qualifications, and hardware evaluations that help bring innovative products to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve real-world engineering challenges by troubleshooting advanced equipment, analyzing process data, and driving improvements in manufacturing performance and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain hands-on experience with cutting-edge tools while collaborating with engineers, technicians, and operators to develop and optimize semiconductor processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make a measurable impact by supporting customer demonstrations, technology evaluations, and continuous improvement initiatives that shape the future of the semiconductor industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with advanced deposition technologies like ALD, PEALD, PECVD, and epitaxy to develop next-gen devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop advanced software for industry-leading semiconductor technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See your code drive the operation of some of the most sophisticated semiconductor equipment in the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a global team of talented software engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the next generation of semiconductor equipment control software and automation technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
