&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;ASM is an equal opportunity employer and considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, nationality, social or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender, gender identify or expression, marital status, pregnancy, political affiliation, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Regional Controller is a finance leadership role responsible for owning financial performance and driving business outcomes within a critical region or Tier 1 customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role goes beyond reporting and analysis — it requires a hands-on operator who takes full ownership of financial results, challenges the business, and drives performance across revenue, margin, cost, and working capital.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Regional Controller operates as the primary finance leader in-region, working directly with business leaders to influence decisions, improve predictability, and ensure strong financial discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this role does not include formal people management, it requires strong day-to-day leadership of regional finance team members. The Regional Controller sets direction, drives execution, and holds the team accountable for results, operating as the functional leader for Finance within the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Culture note: Our finance leaders operate with high ownership, transparency, and accountability. We expect leaders who develop talent, elevate financial rigor, and build a culture of continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Ownership &amp;amp; Performance Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own financial performance for the assigned region or Tier 1 customer, including revenue, margin, cost, inventory, capex investments, and operating expenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary financial authority for the business, ensuring decisions drive sustainable and profitable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify risks and opportunities, driving corrective actions across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead performance discussions with business stakeholders, moving beyond reporting to driving results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Leadership &amp;amp; Accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day leadership and direction to regional finance team members (e.g., analysts or controllers), ensuring clarity of priorities and high-quality execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the single point of accountability for all regional financial outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Address regional performance gaps directly by driving clarity, improving execution, and reinforcing accountability — even without formal reporting lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and enforce a high standard for financial rigor, discipline, and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planning, Forecasting &amp;amp; Financial Control&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own forecast accuracy across revenue, gross margin, OpEx, and working capital&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead annual planning, monthly forecasting, and performance review processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive disciplined variance analysis and ensure proactive follow-through on gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistency and alignment with global Business Control standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Customer Financial Leadership (Tier 1 Focus)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as finance lead for key customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with sales and operations to influence pricing, deal structures, and commercial decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support customer performance reviews and provide financial insight on growth, margin, and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance, Controls &amp;amp; Inventory Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strong financial control and compliance across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee consignment inventory, service parts accounting, and reconciliation accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain adherence to financial policies and IFRS-aligned practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit processes with accurate documentation and timely issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operating in Complex Regional Environments&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate effectively in dynamic and evolving business environments, particularly where processes, data quality, and discipline may vary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish structure, governance, and performance cadence in less mature or rapidly scaling environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive consistency and transparency across regions with varying practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear accountability for financial outcomes across the region or customer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, visible finance leadership recognized by business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improved business performance driven by Finance involvement (not just insight)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-quality, predictable forecasts and disciplined execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regional finance team operating at a consistently high level of performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurable development and capability growth of junior team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scalable, consistent processes across reporting, forecasting, and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of finance experience with demonstrated business ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience supporting operations, supply chain, or customer-facing businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of influencing decisions and driving financial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams informally or formally, with clear evidence of elevating performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and financial modeling capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP systems (SAP preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently in fast-paced, ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA, CPA, CMA, or equivalent advanced credential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in semiconductor, high technology, or manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Tier 1 customers or large strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in global, matrixed organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to pricing, deal structuring, and commercial decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Culture &amp;amp; Leadership Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finance leaders at ASM are expected to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outcomes, not just report results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong business judgment in ambiguous situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead without authority, driving alignment and accountability across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with candor and transparency, using fact-based reasoning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge the business constructively to improve performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement in processes, tools, and capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-impact role supporting critical Tier 1 customers and key regional markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct influence on business performance, strategy, and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to operate as a regional finance leader with visible impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to complex, global semiconductor operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
