&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At ASM, our Manufacturing Engineering team plays a key role in transforming innovative semiconductor equipment designs into scalable, high-quality manufacturing solutions. As an Engineer II, Manufacturing Engineering, you will drive product industrialization, manufacturing readiness, and continuous improvement initiatives across the product lifecycle. Working closely with global cross-functional teams, you will help optimize cost, quality, and operational efficiency while enabling successful product transfers into high-volume manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Marketing, Design Engineering, Special Products, and Refurbishment teams during product development to influence Design for Manufacturing (DFM) decisions and achieve cost targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive manufacturing readiness activities throughout the Product Life Cycle (PLC), from concept and development phases through production release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional initiatives focused on cost reduction, cycle time improvement, quality enhancement, material flow optimization, and manufacturing efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Manufacturing Engineering, Procurement, Materials, NPI, and Operations teams to ensure successful product industrialization and production ramp-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, validate, and continuously improve test and inspection documentation, including test plans, procedures, and inspection checklists for complex modules and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement tooling, automation, and test equipment solutions that improve manufacturing productivity, quality, and consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Manufacturing Readiness Reviews (MRRs) and support Product Transfer Readiness Reviews (PTRRs) to ensure products are successfully transitioned into high-volume manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Mechanical, Electrical, Controls, Software, and Supply Chain teams to develop deep product and system-level expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives using Lean manufacturing principles and operational excellence methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support, knowledge transfer, and training to manufacturing teams, suppliers, and other internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, or a related engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of experience in manufacturing engineering, quality engineering, production engineering, or a related technical environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within the semiconductor equipment, capital equipment, or advanced technology manufacturing industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of manufacturing processes, system integration, assembly, testing, and inspection of complex electro-mechanical equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Bill of Materials (BOM) structures, engineering change processes, and configuration management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Product Life Cycle (PLC) processes, engineering change workflows, and change control requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management, problem-solving, and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working effectively across global and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ERP/MRP systems such as SAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Lean Manufacturing and operational excellence methodologies, including FMEA, 8D, PDCA, DMAIC, Six Sigma, SPC, GR&amp;amp;R, and process capability analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting New Product Introduction (NPI) programs and product transfers into high-volume manufacturing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
