&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Technician&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Process Technician to support engineering and laboratory operations through hands-on execution of metrology activities, wafer and FOUP preparation, equipment monitoring, and routine process support tasks. This individual will play a critical role in enabling efficient laboratory operations by managing multiple requests, supporting engineers across various projects, and ensuring high-quality execution of daily activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is highly organized, service-oriented, and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where priorities may shift throughout the day. Success in this role requires strong attention to detail, effective communication skills, and the ability to balance multiple tasks while maintaining a positive and collaborative attitude.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily laboratory operations by executing metrology measurements and data collection activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform FOUP preparation, wafer handling, and material movement in accordance with established procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run process and metrology jobs on engineering and laboratory equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete scheduled weekly tool monitors and routine equipment health checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist engineers with experiment setup, sample preparation, and data gathering activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform basic tool operation, setup, and minor maintenance activities following documented procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and prioritize multiple work requests from engineers and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accurate documentation of completed work, tool status, and laboratory activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clean, organized, and safe laboratory environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate equipment, process, or safety concerns in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous improvement efforts to enhance laboratory efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate degree, technical certification, or equivalent experience in a laboratory, manufacturing, engineering, or semiconductor environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience following detailed procedures and work instructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and multitasking skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to safely handle wafers, FOUPs, and laboratory materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic computer skills including Microsoft Office applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with engineers and technicians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a semiconductor laboratory or manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with metrology equipment and measurement techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting engineering development activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of process control and equipment monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in cleanroom environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
