&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Technician – ALD Applications &amp;amp; Process Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At ASM, we are advancing semiconductor manufacturing through innovation in Atomic Layer Deposition (ALD) and enabling our customers to develop the next generation of memory, logic, and specialty semiconductor devices. We are seeking a highly motivated Process Technician to join our Applications and Process Development team in a fast-paced laboratory environment supporting leading-edge semiconductor technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the team, you will support process development, customer demonstrations, tool operations, and laboratory activities associated with advanced ALD technologies. The ideal candidate is hands-on, detail-oriented, safety-focused, and thrives in a collaborative environment where priorities can change quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and maintain advanced ALD deposition systems supporting process development, customer demonstrations, and technology qualification activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform wafer handling, sample preparation, process execution, and post-process metrology activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute process experiments, collect process data, and maintain accurate experimental records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor tool performance and assist in routine preventative maintenance, troubleshooting, and recovery activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support chamber qualification, process characterization, and tool matching activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in tool ownership activities, Best Known Method (BKM) development, laboratory sustaining, and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to all safety protocols involving semiconductor process equipment, chemicals, gases, and facility systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in cross-training across multiple process modules and characterization techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Ideal Candidate Will Demonstrate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a dynamic environment with changing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and commitment to quality execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent troubleshooting and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a multidisciplinary team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to interface with engineers, technicians, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong safety mindset and commitment to laboratory best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous learning mindset and interest in advanced semiconductor technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High School diploma; OR&amp;nbsp;Associate degree, technical certification, military technical training, or equivalent experience in Engineering Technology, Electronics, Materials Science, Chemistry, Physics, Mechanical Engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to follow detailed procedures, experimental plans, and safety protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of hands-on experience in semiconductor manufacturing, semiconductor equipment, process development laboratories, or a related high-technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating semiconductor process equipment in a production, engineering, or R&amp;amp;D setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of semiconductor wafer processing and contamination control practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience with tool ownership, process transfer, equipment qualification, or process sustainment activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
