&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a HR Business Partner in ASM, you are part of the Global HR team. This role reports to the Global HR Business Partner of Global Operations based in Singapore and is responsible and accountable for delivering HR-business solutions to the Global Operations teams based in Singapore &amp;amp; Malaysia. You will also support and collaborate with Global &amp;amp; Regional HR Business Partners&amp;nbsp;and HR Center of Excellence (CoEs) for Global &amp;amp; Regional initiatives to be implemented and executed in Singapore and Malaysia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires both strategic thinking as well as tactical and hands on execution in a dynamic and demanding business environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Global HR Business Partner and assigned Business Leaders to drive HR initiatives for the assigned Business Units – Global Operations (GOPS) - in Singapore &amp;amp; Malaysia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with senior leaders to plan, implement, and execute people-related initiatives and programs that support business growth and strategic objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead key initiatives related to talent, leadership, organizational development, performance management and culture transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the adoption and implementation of regional and global HR Center of Excellence (COE) programs for GOPS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide data-driven insights, analysis, and recommendations to address HR queries, inform decision-making, and enhance organizational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
