&lt;p&gt;As a Global Planning Process Lead, you will strengthen ASM’s global planning capabilities by shaping standards that support our long-term growth and operational excellence. You will work closely with global process owners, IT, and cross-functional teams to enhance system performance (SAP, Kinaxis), drive harmonization, and elevate planning efficiency across regions. Your work will help ensure that our supply chain is resilient, data-driven, and ready for what’s next in the semiconductor industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end process mapping and standardization efforts, simplifying workflows and translating business requirements into scalable digital capabilities and solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own global planning process standards and the associated business capability roadmap, driving alignment from process design through implementation, adoption, and sustainment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and prioritize business requirements for end-to-end planning solutions, partnering with IT, vendors, and business stakeholders to support solution design, configuration, integration, testing, and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and govern master data standards, business rules, process controls, performance measures, and traceability requirements to enable safety, quality, delivery, cost, and productivity objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Manufacturing and Logistics teams to optimize end-to-end processes and improve operational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure planning system capabilities align with enterprise process standards, digital platform strategy, and target-state business process design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with global process owners, functional leaders, and IT teams to continuously enhance system capabilities, improve user adoption, and advance process and platform maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure planning processes, controls, and system configurations comply with corporate policies, regulatory requirements, and audit standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide data-driven insights and recommendations to leadership on process performance, standardization opportunities, capability gaps, and continuous improvement priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives that leverage process, system, and operational data to increase efficiency, visibility, decision quality, and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree or Bachelor’s degree in Supply Chain, Business Administration, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 10 years of experience in planning or supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in SAP S/4HANA and Kinaxis Supply Chain Management solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge in supply chain and procurement operations process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to work across time zones and cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving mindset with experience in fast-paced, high-mix environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading global transformation initiatives with SAP S4HANA and/or Kinaxis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with advanced supply chain models and digital procurement tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence and drive alignment in a global matrix structure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills for sharing insights with leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
