&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manager II, Field Process (Technical Manager)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead customer process engagement, new product introduction (NPI), and successful transition to high volume manufacturing (HVM). Drive process performance, resolve technical escalations, enhance customer satisfaction, and cross-functional execution while building a high-performing field process engineering team&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer &amp;amp; Technical Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong customer relationships and serve as a trusted technical advisor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate customer technology and process needs to support long-term growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a field process team responsible for process development, qualification, optimization, and troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Own and drive critical customer escalations through timely resolution&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPI &amp;amp; HVM Programs Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead NPI programs through qualification and successful HVM adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure on-time delivery of process and product milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process performance, tool uptime, and customer success in HVM transition phase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with ASM R&amp;amp;D, Product Engineering, KPU, Business Units, Field Service, and Sales teams to execute technology programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align stakeholders on priorities, action plans, and execution timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide customer feedback to improve product and process performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support technology roadmap development with internal and customer teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership / Business &amp;amp; Strategic Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, mentor, and develop high-performing process engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of safety, accountability, urgency, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a team capable of independently solving complex technical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support business growth through successful technology adoption and customer satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create visibility into key technical issues and drive execution across organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PHD or Master’s degree in Physics, Chemistry, Materials Science, Electrical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;12+ years of experience with a Bachelor&#39;s degree, 9+ years with a Master&#39;s degree, or 6+ years with a PhD in the semiconductor industry, with strong expertise in thin-film processes such as PEALD, PECVD, LPCVD, ALD, Epitaxy, or Vertical Furnace&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Proven ability to manage new product and process introduction, as well as the transfer of complex deposition processes and hardware from R&amp;amp;D to HVM.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management, analytical, and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership with a proven track record of driving and implementing organizational change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Proactively manage escalations, develop action plans, and maintain clear communication among customers, service teams, business units, and external suppliers&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as needed, including extended periods for training and technical engagement with the Business Unit and customer sites.&amp;nbsp; The primary customer focus will be onsite in Boise, Idaho&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Strong understanding of intellectual property boundaries between ASM and customers, with the ability to maintain appropriate IP protection during all internal and external interactions&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working effectively with local, regional, and global teams, with strong cross-functional and cross-division collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;5-10 years of broad semiconductor technical experience combined with strong business acumen. Experience in Memory (DRAM and Advanced Memory) and/or Advanced Packaging is highly desirable.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience working for a semiconductor equipment supplier, a strong customer-focused mindset, and prior people management experience are strong advantages.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
