&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job&#39;s mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Field Service is responsible for leading customer-facing service operations and post-sales support activities for strategic semiconductor customers. This role drives customer satisfaction, operational excellence, and business performance while leading a team of service leaders and field service professionals supporting ASM&#39;s advanced semiconductor manufacturing equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the primary service leader and customer interface, this individual collaborates closely with customer executives, ASM leadership, product teams, and cross-functional stakeholders to ensure successful service delivery, strengthen customer relationships, and support long-term business growth. The Senior Manager, Field Service plays a critical role in workforce planning, organizational development, operational performance, and strategic account support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop Service Operations Managers, Field Service Managers, and Field Service Engineers supporting strategic semiconductor customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture where safety, quality, collaboration, and accountability are top priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong customer relationships at both operational and executive levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary service escalation point for critical customer issues and business concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive customer satisfaction through effective service delivery, issue resolution, and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead workforce planning activities to ensure organizational readiness and alignment with customer demand and business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop leadership and technical talent pipelines through coaching, mentoring, succession planning, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Units, Product Marketing, Business Development, and Support teams to drive successful customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and improve operational performance through the analysis of service metrics, business indicators, and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive service operational excellence through process improvements, resource optimization, and execution discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support service and business forecasting activities while ensuring alignment to organizational objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence business decisions through clear, concise, and data-driven communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong partnerships with suppliers, customers, and internal stakeholders to ensure business continuity and customer success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent ASM as a senior service leader during executive customer engagements and strategic business discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development and execution of strategic initiatives that support revenue growth, operational performance, and customer retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering or related technical discipline required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in the semiconductor industry supporting complex capital equipment and advanced process technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of leadership experience managing technical teams, service organizations, or customer-facing operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting semiconductor manufacturing customers in a service, operations, account management, or customer success capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading cross-functional teams and managing complex customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to independently manage complex projects, customer engagements, and organizational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of semiconductor equipment service operations and customer support environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing operational strategies that support business growth and customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills with the ability to influence technical teams, customers, and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to leverage data to drive business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel domestically and internationally as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading customer-facing service organizations within the semiconductor capital equipment industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success managing strategic customer relationships and executive-level engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving operational excellence, workforce planning, and service transformation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen with experience supporting revenue growth, operational performance, and customer retention strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional teams and drive alignment across complex organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing future leaders and building high-performing service organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of semiconductor manufacturing environments, customer support models, and post-sales service strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of delivering measurable improvements in customer satisfaction, service quality, and operational effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
