&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job&#39;s mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the NPI Field Service team responsible for first-of-kind tool installations, beta evaluations, customer-site qualifications, and transfer of new products into high-volume manufacturing support. The manager will build team capability, drive execution across customer and factory stakeholders, resolve escalations, and ensure safe, predictable, and repeatable deployment of new semiconductor equipment platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of NPI Field Service Engineers supporting first-of-kind tool installations, RFKs, beta evaluations, technology demonstrations, and other NPI activities at customer sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own field service execution for factory readiness reviews, installation planning, startup, qualification, and customer acceptance milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish resource, coverage, travel, training, and succession plans aligned with the NPI roadmap and customer deployment schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive safe and disciplined execution, including compliance with company, customer, and site requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership during complex hardware, and integration issues encountered during startup and qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with NPI Field Process Engineering to achieve hardware and process readiness and to align priorities, dependencies, and recovery plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functionally with Product teams, GPS, Manufacturing, R&amp;amp;D, Quality, Supply Chain, and local service organizations to close product and execution gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer technical reviews and service-related escalation meetings; communicate status, risk, containment, recovery plans, and executive-level updates clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track operational metrics for installation progress, qualification readiness, issue closure, repeat failures, documentation maturity, and transfer readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure structured problem-solving, root-cause analysis, corrective actions, and lessons learned are completed for critical field issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive development and standardization of installation procedures, troubleshooting guides, startup checklists, service documentation, and knowledge-management practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify product, serviceability, reliability, tooling, spare-parts, and documentation gaps; provide prioritized field feedback to engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build technical capability through coaching, mentoring, hands-on reviews, and training programs for NPI and local service teams.&lt;/li&gt;
