&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Materials Science, Physics, Mechatronics, or a related discipline is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in one of the above disciplines with substantial semiconductor equipment, field service, process engineering, or NPI experience will also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous people-management, technical-leadership, or team-lead experience in a customer-facing semiconductor equipment environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading NPI, technology development, beta evaluations, first-of-kind installations, or transfer of new equipment into production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead teams through complex troubleshooting, customer escalations, changing priorities, and unclear ownership paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of semiconductor equipment systems, including vacuum systems, gas delivery, RF power, plasma systems, automation and robotics, and ALD, PEALD, PECVD, furnace, or related deposition platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with installation and qualification planning, operational readiness, structured problem-solving, root-cause analysis, and corrective-action management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate technical detail into clear priorities, risk assessments, recovery plans, and executive-level communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder-management, coaching, decision-making, communication, and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-focused leadership style with the ability to balance urgency, technical rigor, employee development, and sustainable execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work across cultures, functions, and time zones and to travel internationally based on business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
