&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering, Materials Science, Physics, Chemistry, Manufacturing, or a related STEM field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in semiconductor manufacturing, advanced technology manufacturing, or a similar technical environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading technical teams, projects, or manufacturing operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to solve complex operational or technical challenges in a fast-paced production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and coaching employees through structured training and capability-building programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Lean Manufacturing, Six Sigma, or other continuous improvement methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and stakeholder management skills with the ability to influence across organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
