&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Engineer, you will lead the successful industrialization and lifecycle support of semiconductor capital equipment by serving as the critical link between Business Units and Operations, driving New Product Introduction (NPI) and sustained products alike for manufacturing readiness, supplier alignment, and continuous improvement initiatives. Enable scalable, cost-effective, and high-quality production through strong technical leadership in DFM, process optimization, root cause problem solving, tooling development, and cross-functional collaboration, while advancing operational excellence across quality, productivity, and efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary engineering interface between Business Units (BU) and Global Operations (GOPS) for assigned the product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support New Product Introduction (NPI) activities from development through production ramp-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide executive-level insights on manufacturing feasibility, cost, and schedules to shape ASM’s manufacturing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manufacturing &amp;amp; Process Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce cutting-edge manufacturing technologies and methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and document manufacturing procedures, build sequences, test plans, and inspection standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Design for Manufacturing (DFM) assessments and provide actionable recommendations to improve manufacturability, quality, and labor/cost efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver tooling and test equipment solutions that meet product requirements while optimizing productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive supplier and contract manufacturer alignment to support successful product launches and ramp-up activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production Support &amp;amp; Operational Excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve complex technical and strategic challenges with a positive, solution-focused mindset in high-pressure settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support production teams in root cause investigations, ensuring timely containment and implementation of corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Design of Experiments (DOE), analyze technical findings, and present recommendations to support manufacturing improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives focused on quality, throughput, efficiency, and cost reduction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Knowledge Sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster technical collaboration and knowledge sharing across engineering, operations, field support, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior engineers, fostering a culture of innovation and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical, Electrical, Electronics, Materials, or Manufacturing Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 8 years of experience in a manufacturing or engineering environment, preferably within the semiconductor capital equipment industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of assembly, integration, and testing of complex systems, preferably within CVD, ALD, or Epitaxy applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in applying Design for Manufacturing (DFM) and Lean Manufacturing principles to improve manufacturability and workflow efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
