&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands-on full-cycle recruiting experience for professional level roles and new college graduates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high volume recruiting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with university recruiting, early career hiring, internships, and/or graduate talent programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong network-building capabilities across universities, research institutes, professors, and emerging talent communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the Asia talent market, particularly STEM and engineering talent pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management and project execution skills with the ability to influence across functions and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable, self-driven, and comfortable navigating ambiguity in a fast-paced regional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-level English required; Mandarin Chinese strongly preferred. Japanese and/or Korean are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Semiconductor, engineering, advanced manufacturing, or technology industry experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
