&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: Materials Handling Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Location: Phoenix, AZ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Materials Handling Specialist, you will support lab development and customer evaluation programs by ensuring materials are available, tracked, and delivered on time. You’ll partner closely with project management, engineering, and supply chain teams to keep critical projects on schedule and maintain smooth material flow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Working On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report material status for lab development projects and customer evaluation units&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with demand planning and supply chain to manage lead times and priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expedite parts Through buyers to meet project timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage and prepare hardware with receiving and inventory teams for lab installations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with project managers, engineering, and product support on development timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular updates on delivery timelines and material readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Submit purchase requisitions and ensure timely conversion to purchase orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track long lead-time items and escalate risks impacting delivery schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or associate degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in supply chain, materials management, or a lab/manufacturing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SAP, purchasing processes, or bill of materials (BOMs) preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read engineering drawings or specifications is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and communication skills with attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Excel for data tracking and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join ASM?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work at the forefront of semiconductor innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with global, cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain exposure to lab and product development environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow your career in a fast-paced, high-impact role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
