&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Senior Field Process Engineer (Richardson, TX)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At ASM, we are shaping the future of semiconductor technology by enabling breakthroughs that power AI, advanced computing, electric vehicles, and next-generation electronics. We are seeking a Senior Field Process Engineer to serve as the on-site epitaxy process expert at a key customer location in Richardson, Texas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Located in the heart of the Dallas-Fort Worth technology corridor, Richardson offers a thriving semiconductor and engineering ecosystem, exceptional career growth opportunities, and access to world-class dining, entertainment, and outdoor recreation. With a strong concentration of technology companies and a lower cost of living than many major tech hubs, Richardson provides an ideal environment for both professional and personal growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Field Process Engineer, you will lead process development, technology transfers, and new product introductions on ASM epitaxy systems at a strategic customer site. You will act as the primary technical liaison between the customer’s engineering teams and ASM&#39;s global product and R&amp;amp;D organizations, ensuring successful process development, qualification, and manufacturing ramp activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This customer-facing role requires strong technical expertise, project leadership, and exceptional communication skills to drive customer success and long-term partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll be working on&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Process Development &amp;amp; Customer Support&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead on-site process development, optimization, and troubleshooting activities on ASM epitaxy systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, execute, and analyze experiments to support new process development, continuous improvement initiatives, tool matching, and issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with customer engineering teams to understand current and future technology requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process and hardware improvements that enhance performance, yield, and customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead new product evaluations, installations, and qualification activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage technical projects from planning through successful execution and customer acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain technical documentation, best practices, and process knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives that enhance customer experience, operational efficiency, and engineering support capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Technology Transfer &amp;amp; Knowledge Management&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead process transfers from ASM R&amp;amp;D organizations to customer qualification and manufacturing sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support technology transfers between manufacturing facilities, including greenfield fabs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document process learnings, hardware improvements, and best known methods (BKMs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transfer product and process knowledge to local service and engineering teams to ensure sustainable customer success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Customer Engagement &amp;amp; Escalation Management&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted technical advisor and primary process interface for the customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage technical escalations and drive structured problem-solving efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop action plans and coordinate communication across customers, service teams, product units, and suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver timely, clear, and professional communication through presentations, reports, and customer meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M.S. or Ph.D. in Materials Science, Chemical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, Physical Chemistry, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of semiconductor process engineering experience, or an equivalent combination of education and industry experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of epitaxial deposition processes, thin-film characterization, semiconductor devices, and vacuum systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and executing experiments using DOE methodologies and statistical analysis techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot complex process and equipment issues using structured problem-solving tools such as KT, FMEA, 7-Step, or Ishikawa methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, customer-facing, and project management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and effectively manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with semiconductor capital equipment and customer-facing engineering roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success developing and optimizing epitaxial deposition processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with ASM epitaxy equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting technology transfers, process qualification, and manufacturing ramp activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Travel Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25% for training, technical collaboration, customer support, and engagement with ASM global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to support critical customer escalations, qualifications, or project milestones, which may occasionally require extended hours or weekend support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
