&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job&#39;s mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Field Service Engineer at ASM, you will play a critical role in supporting our customers by installing, maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing advanced semiconductor capital equipment. You will serve as a technical expert in the field, partnering closely with customers and internal teams to ensure equipment performance, reliability, and uptime. This role offers the opportunity to work with cutting-edge semiconductor technology while supporting leading semiconductor manufacturers across domestic and international locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position may be filled on either a day shift or night shift schedule based on business needs. Day shift operates Monday through Friday from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM. Night shift positions operate Monday through Friday from 6:00 PM to 2:00 AM and are dedicated to supporting customer operations during overnight production hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform installation, qualification, preventive maintenance, and repair activities on complex semiconductor capital equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve electrical, electronic, mechanical, and software-related equipment issues in customer manufacturing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support and training to customers while maintaining a high level of customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret and utilize electrical and electro-mechanical schematics, drawings, and technical documentation to diagnose equipment issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support equipment upgrades, modifications, and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document service activities, maintenance actions, and technical findings accurately and thoroughly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, technical support, and customer teams to resolve complex technical issues and improve equipment performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to all safety procedures and maintain a safety-first mindset while working within semiconductor manufacturing facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work either a day shift schedule (Monday through Friday, 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM) or a night shift schedule (Monday through Friday, 6:00 PM to 2:00 AM), depending on position assignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel domestically and internationally (25%-75%) to support customer installations, upgrades, and service requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electronics, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electro-Mechanical Technology, or a related technical discipline, or equivalent military technical training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of field service, customer support, semiconductor manufacturing, or related experience supporting complex capital equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting skills with microprocessor-controlled electro-mechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret electrical, electronic, and electro-mechanical schematics and drawings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing preventive maintenance, installations, repairs, and system diagnostics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of oscilloscopes, digital voltmeters (DVMs), and other diagnostic tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and effectively in a team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-focused with a positive and professional approach to service and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting semiconductor capital equipment in wafer fabrication environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of vacuum systems, closed-loop gas control systems, and electro-pneumatic controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RF plasma technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with robotics, motion control systems, and microprocessor-based controllers.&lt;/li&gt;
