&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready for your next move at ASM?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You already know what makes ASM special: our people, our purpose, and our passion for innovation. Now’s your chance to grow your career from the inside, take on new challenges, and shape what’s next with us.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Engineer, Field Service, you will serve as an internal escalation lead, using deep system‑level expertise to resolve the most complex technical challenges across multiple ASM toolsets. You will guide root‑cause analysis, prevent recurrence, and collaborate closely with engineering, design, and customer teams to enhance stability, performance, and efficiency. Your leadership strengthens our service organization, elevates field capability, and drives improvements that directly support ASM’s mission of enabling the world’s most advanced semiconductor technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead internal escalations and root‑cause investigations for complex, multi‑factor technical issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose system interactions across mechanical, electrical, software, and process‑integration domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify performance trends in areas such as gas delivery, thermal control, and process deviations, and drive resolution with Field Service Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor peers on advanced diagnostic strategies and contribute to improvements in troubleshooting protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise safety procedures, provide team training, and support internal and external safety audits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map unit‑process variables to device physics and design DOEs to enhance yield and stability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select appropriate measurement techniques for sensitivity and sample constraints and troubleshoot instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate escalations, quantify technical and operational risk, and prevent issue recurrence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align customer needs with design constraints and draft upgrade proposals spanning multiple fabs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex escalations while balancing production pressure and technical risk, and capture lessons learned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Electrical, Mechanical, Electromechanical Engineering or related field with 6+ years of experience, OR a Master’s degree with 4+ years of experience OR PhD degree with 0+ years of experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of tool architecture, process interactions, and advanced system‑level troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading root‑cause investigations and cross‑functional escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret complex schematics and diagnose issues involving multiple engineering disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supervising safety compliance and supporting audit activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to clearly articulate complex issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and lead teams in high‑pressure situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel domestically and internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with MS Office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in gas delivery, thermal control, vacuum systems, plasma, RF, or instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mapping process variables to device physics and designing DOEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background coordinating cross‑site escalations or multi‑fab upgrade initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence customers and guide discussions during high‑impact technical escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring peers and shaping troubleshooting methodologies&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
