&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Field Service Engineer at ASM, you will support one of our key customers as they push the boundaries of the most advanced&amp;nbsp;technology&amp;nbsp;nodes in semiconductor manufacturing.&amp;nbsp;You will&amp;nbsp;become part of a diverse, global team united by curiosity, precision, and a shared drive to stay ahead of&amp;nbsp;what’s next. Based on site&amp;nbsp;in Lucan, this role offers an excellent foundation for early career&amp;nbsp;engineers, or an opportunity to deepen your&amp;nbsp;expertise in a high-tech environment that values safety, learning agility, and technical excellence. You will receive extensive training through ASM’s Global Training Center, alongside hands-on&amp;nbsp;mentorship from experienced ASM engineers. Your work will directly&amp;nbsp;impact&amp;nbsp;tool performance, uptime, and customer satisfaction; making you an essential part of&amp;nbsp;the customer&amp;nbsp;experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute installation, decommissioning, preventative maintenance, and repair of advanced electromechanical semiconductor equipment at Key Customer sites globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate strong ownership through effective troubleshooting, precise problem-solving, and ensuring tools return to&amp;nbsp;optimal&amp;nbsp;performance efficiently.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain&amp;nbsp;high levels&amp;nbsp;of customer satisfaction by providing&amp;nbsp;timely updates, clear communication, and high-quality&amp;nbsp;technical solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct structured customer training, ensuring safe, clear, and&amp;nbsp;well documented&amp;nbsp;handovers and support.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent ASM professionally through proactive communication, reliability, and a solutions-oriented approach- strengthening long-term&amp;nbsp;customer trust.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross functionally&amp;nbsp;with regional and global engineering teams to escalate issues appropriately, share insights, and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to strict safety and quality protocols, ensuring all service activities meet cleanroom and equipment standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or master’s degree in mechanical, Electrical, Electronic, or Mechatronic Engineering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of electrical and gas schematics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mechanical and electrical troubleshooting skills with a disciplined, safety-first&amp;nbsp;mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication skills and the ability to function within cross functional&amp;nbsp;and multicultural teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid organizational and problem-solving&amp;nbsp;skills, with the ability to prioritize work in a dynamic environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advantageous experience in one or more of the following areas:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Semiconductor wafer&amp;nbsp;fab&amp;nbsp;operations / Vacuum and gas control systems / RF plasma systems / Electropneumatic controls / Microprocessor based&amp;nbsp;controllers / Robotics / Handling of toxic/flammable gases and chemicals&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel internationally (typically 75%, mainly to the U.S &amp;amp; Europe).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to attend a product training at ASM’s Global HQ in the US.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have valid authorization to work in Ireland and the EU.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At ASM,&amp;nbsp;you’ll&amp;nbsp;join a&amp;nbsp;diverse&amp;nbsp;team of engineers and innovators who support each other, share knowledge openly, and continuously develop through worldclass training.&amp;nbsp;You’ll&amp;nbsp;experience an environment built on trust, curiosity, and teamwork, while gaining exposure to the world’s most advanced semiconductor technologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your package with us&amp;nbsp;will include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance based bonus program&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension scheme and private health insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gym and daily meal allowance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive technical training opportunities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Longterm career pathways across regions, technologies, and disciplines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educational support for continued professional development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
