&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop mechanical systems and components for advanced node Atomic Layer Deposition equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply sound engineering principles, fundamentals of physics, and product-focused mindset to meet customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform engineering calculations related to structural, thermal, and fluid dynamics to support robust and reliable designs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain Creo Parametric 3D CAD models and complex assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate 2D drawings, applying GD&amp;amp;T standards (ASME Y14.5 and/or ISO 1101) for use in a global supply chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate the feasibility of product proposals, resolve technical issues, and develop&amp;nbsp;new designs&amp;nbsp;in compliance with product safety and customer need&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare complete engineering documentation to support prototype to HVM transition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support engineering project activities, including design characterization, schedule planning, design reviews, and coordination with&amp;nbsp;cross‑functional&amp;nbsp;teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish&amp;nbsp;and maintain product structures and configurations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in and present at design reviews for&amp;nbsp;new designs, product enhancements, and&amp;nbsp;customer‑specific&amp;nbsp;solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hardware development, installation, and testing to verify performance; create, review, and approve test plans and test procedures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with manufacturing, suppliers, and other engineering teams to ensure smooth product transfer into the manufacturing cycle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and process engineering change requests (ECR/ECO) and support continuous product and process improvements&amp;nbsp; through Teamcenter PLM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to customer or supplier sites as needed to support technical discussions and project execution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a strong commitment to safety in all activities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we are looking for&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in mechanical engineering or&amp;nbsp;related&amp;nbsp;disciplines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of&amp;nbsp;hands‑on&amp;nbsp;experience in mechanical design and development of complex systems within semiconductor or capital equipment industries.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with mechanical systems such as vacuum chambers, reactors,&amp;nbsp;susceptor heaters,&amp;nbsp;gas delivery systems, pneumatics, cooling&amp;nbsp;circuits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform simulation and engineering analysis (e.g., structural, thermal, fluid dynamics) to support robust and reliable designs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency&amp;nbsp;in Creo (or equivalent CAD tools) and ability to create detailed engineering drawings&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of materials, manufacturing processes, and mechanical design fundamentals for use in vacuum and ultra clean processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong&amp;nbsp;problem‑solving&amp;nbsp;skills and creativity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work effectively in a&amp;nbsp;cross‑functional,&amp;nbsp;fast‑paced&amp;nbsp;environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What sets you apart&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD&amp;nbsp;in Mechanical Engineering or related degree. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with thermal and plasma-based deposition equipment (ALD, PEALD, CVD)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems level design and characterization, bridging component design to over-all system and on-wafer performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong capability to run and interpret&amp;nbsp;multiphysics&amp;nbsp;simulations (structural, thermal, CFD) and apply the results to improve design specifications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extremely large CAD assembly management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong dFX and DFMEA experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing core reactor hardware (susceptors, showerheads, RF delivery, etc)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting products through the full lifecycle, from concept and design to manufacturing release.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently manage technical tasks while contributing effectively as a team player.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
