&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Engineer II, Key Account Technology (KAT) at ASM, you will serve as a key technical interface for strategic customers, driving new technology introduction and ensuring successful deployment of epitaxy (Epi) processes in high-volume manufacturing environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines deep process expertise with strong customer engagement, supporting NPI, resolving complex technical escalations, and influencing product development through direct customer insight. You will work closely with both customer R&amp;amp;D/manufacturing teams and ASM global teams to enable long-term technology success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Selected candidates will participate in approximately 6 months of training in the United States to build deep understanding of ASM technology and product platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Act as the primary technical interface for key customers, supporting Epitaxy process development and production while building strong relationships with customer R&amp;amp;D and manufacturing teams&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Drive NPI and evaluation activities at customer sites, leading hands-on deployment and implementing BU-developed BKMs and process improvements&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Execute and support customer-specific DOE and demo activities in collaboration with process teams&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Diagnose and resolve complex process and equipment issues across development and production environments, while leading technical escalations including root cause analysis and corrective actions&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Monitor equipment performance and ensure alignment with customer specifications&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
