&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job&#39;s mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;R&amp;amp;D Process Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; at ASM, you will play a key role in developing and optimizing advanced semiconductor deposition processes that enable next-generation devices.&lt;br&gt;You will work hands-on with state-of-the-art processing and analytical equipment, contributing to innovation in &lt;strong&gt;ALD/PEALD, PECVD, CVD, Epitaxy, oxidation, annealing, and curing processes&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;This role offers the opportunity to turn scientific ideas into impactful technologies through process development, customer engagement, and intellectual property creation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Researching, developing, and optimizing thin film deposition processes, with a focus on &lt;strong&gt;metal and dielectric films using PEALD and related technologies&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Designing and executing complex experiments using&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Design of Experiments (DOE)&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Response Surface Methodology (RSM)&lt;/strong&gt;, and interpreting experimental results.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Developing new film materials and processes for emerging semiconductor applications based on strong chemistry and materials science fundamentals.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Actively troubleshooting process and equipment issues through hands-on engagement.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Participating in and driving structured technical problem-solving using scientific methodologies and industry tools.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Collaborating with customers and central marketing to define requirements and execute customer demonstrations.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Supporting product transfer to customers by delivering demonstrations, training field service teams, creating technical documentation, and traveling to customer sites (up to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;10%&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Authoring technical papers and contributing to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;intellectual property (IP)&lt;/strong&gt; generation related to process and technology development.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
