&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PhD&lt;/strong&gt; in Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field &lt;em&gt;or&lt;/em&gt; &lt;strong&gt;MS degree with 2+ years of relevant industry experience&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Hands-on experience with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;PEALD, ALD, PECVD, CVD, Epitaxy&lt;/strong&gt;, or other thin film deposition technologies.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Strong understanding of thin film deposition principles and semiconductor process development.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience designing and characterizing deposition processes using first principles and experimental design techniques.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Ability to independently manage complex process development activities.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Excellent communication skills in &lt;strong&gt;English and Korean&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to clearly explain complex technical concepts.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;electrical characterization techniques for CMOS devices&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience integrating metal and/or dielectric films into&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;FEOL and BEOL process flows&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Hands-on experience with materials characterization techniques such as&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;XPS, SIMS, AFM, XRD, TEM, SEM, Raman, or ellipsometry&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience authoring technical publications and/or patents in the semiconductor industry.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
