&lt;p&gt;-Bachelor’s degree or higher in Computer Science, Electrical/Mechanical Engineering, or a related field&lt;br&gt;-3+ years of relevant work experience&lt;br&gt;-Solid understanding of object-oriented programming using C++ or C#&lt;br&gt;-Ability to communicate effectively in English (documentation and collaboration)&lt;br&gt;-Strong sense of ownership and proactive work attitude&lt;br&gt;-Team-oriented mindset with positive collaboration skills&lt;br&gt;-Even if your experience does not match every requirement, we encourage you to apply if you are eager to learn and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
