&lt;p&gt;ASM is a leading, global supplier of semiconductor process equipment for wafer processing. We deliver innovative technology solutions to the world’s leading semiconductor manufacturers.&amp;nbsp; We are a dynamic, growing company and provide groundbreaking solutions that are helping to make semiconductor devices smaller, faster, and more powerful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ASM International NV is headquartered in the Netherlands. Our over 4,700 employees are based in 14 countries, including the United States, Europe, Japan, Korea, Taiwan, and Singapore. We benefit from this diverse perspective and the advantages of bringing together the best brains in the world to create new breakthroughs, turning today’s challenges into tomorrow’s opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a software development engineer, you will develop control software for ASM semiconductor equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading and improving the SQA process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, recommend, and implement automated testing tools and strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research new tools, technologies, and testing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and enhance the functionality of our internally developed (C#) modeling engine testing tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design test plans, scenarios, scripts, or procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document software defects, using a bug tracking system, and report defects to software developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, analyze, and document problems with program function, output, online screen, or content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document test procedures to ensure replicability and compliance with standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and English communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team player who enjoys supporting and working with others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;S in Computer Science or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with UI/BDD and end-to-end testing tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 4 years of professional experience in software development or automation engineering, or similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in software development using C++ and C#&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in development and usage of Git, SVN, or Jira.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working as part of a Scrum or other Agile software team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience in utilizing automation tools (WinAppDriver, SmartBear TestComplete).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;More than 4 years of experience in the semiconductor industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in developing automation tools and writing test cases.&lt;/li&gt;
