&lt;p&gt;A senior level engineer responsible for organizing and researching proposed product base lines, including product changes, releases, and obsolescence. In this role, you will serve as the Product Change Lead&amp;nbsp;for a specific product line. Your primary responsibility will be to implement product changes across the enterprise, overseeing the entire process from the initial change proposal to execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the global product baseline and change process within a designated business unit, ensuring successful implementation across assigned product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand product baselines and change control requirements for assigned products and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify components and assemblies critically to implementing product changes at operational sites and within both existing and new customer-installed bases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead programs and various projects and partner with stakeholders to develop efficient product change management processes that improve cycle time, enhance manufacturing execution, and &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; minimize inventory impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide product support to manufacturing, supply chain, product management, account management, and other functional teams regarding baselines and modifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate expertise in product change processes and related business practices, including proficiency with enterprise systems such as PLM and ERP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee planning functions to ensure effective change of implementation dates and smooth transitions across operational sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with engineering documentation standards and maintain accuracy in Bill of Materials (BOM) management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Digital Mockup (DMU) and iteration modeling instances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in mechanical or industrial engineering, or equivalent industry experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of experience managing complex technical programs and engineering projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years in product configuration and systems engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong exposure to Configuration Management (CMII) practices (CMII certification preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of Project Management principles (PMI foundation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of inventory management and CPIM practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PLM systems (e.g., Teamcenter) and ERP systems (SAP S4 Hana, MRP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in 3D CAD environments (CREO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Design for Six Sigma methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Skills Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate knowledge of complex mechanical/electrical model systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong analytical skills with the ability to break down complex problems into actionable components.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Ability to work effectively in a matrix environment, driving results and influencing change through collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
