&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Systems Engineering, or a related engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of experience in field service, technical support, or global product support within the semiconductor industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting semiconductor manufacturing equipment and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong system-level troubleshooting and structured problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on engineering capability, with the ability to connect engineering principles to real-world equipment behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data analysis and structured problem-solving methods to investigate technical issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including experience in customer-facing technical discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively across global teams and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel internationally ~ 25 to 50% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
