&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join ASM&#39;s growing Key Account Technology team, where you&#39;ll help drive product innovation, strengthen strategic customer partnerships, and support the successful adoption of next-generation ALD technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Key Account Technologist (KAT), you will serve as a trusted technical advisor to customers, supporting new product introductions, product enhancements, and product modifications while helping secure Development Tool of Record (DTOR) wins and optimizing installed base performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with customers and cross-functional teams, you will help shape ASM&#39;s ALD technology roadmap, address technical challenges, and ensure customer requirements are translated into effective product and process solutions. Success in this role requires strong technical expertise, customer engagement, collaboration, and a proactive approach to Product Life Cycle (PLC) management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead process application NPI (New Product Introduction), product improvements, and product modifications across the Key Product Unit (KPU) installed base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain strong relationships with key customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary technical interface for assigned customer accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive resolution of process and hardware-related escalations in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, maintain, and implement Best Known Method (BKM) processes for process applications, including standards, specifications, recipes, and installed base performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with ASM customer account teams and customer engineering organizations to ensure customer requirements are understood and addressed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive collaboration with key internal stakeholders, including Process Development, Global Sales, Service &amp;amp; Spares, Account Teams, Engineering, and Global Product Management (GPM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;KEY SELECTION CRITERIA&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience (or 3+ years with a Ph.D.) in the semiconductor wafer processing or capital equipment industry preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree or above in Materials Science, Physics, Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in process engineering, productivity, or similar technical customer-facing roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and maintain trusted, long-term customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including presentation and influencing abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Semiconductor industry experience focused primarily on thin film deposition and treatment - Atomic Layer Deposition (ALD) and/or Chemical Vapor Deposition (CVD), etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with work function metals, metallization, silicides, and electrode applications in logic and/or memory is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PERSONAL / PROFESSIONAL ATTRIBUTES&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter with high energy and a strong work ethic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly motivated and results driven.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive change agent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker with the ability to translate strategy into execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem solver who communicates effectively and navigates challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to make sound decisions independently and execute with urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead and influence across cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative with strong relationship-building and conflict management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;TRAVEL&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to travel internationally up to 30% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
