&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience / Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in a high-tech, complex industry environment (e.g., semiconductor, advanced equipment, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in leading change and driving results in fast-paced, dynamic environments, including product introductions or innovation cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mindset with the ability to independently drive initiatives and deliver results under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence and align stakeholders across functions and seniority levels, even without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid leadership and coaching capabilities, with experience developing high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a hands-on approach to identifying issues and driving improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills in English (verbal &amp;amp; written), with the ability to clearly present complex concepts to diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage escalations, resolve critical issues, and rebuild customer confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced, matrixed, and multicultural environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and multitasking skills, with the ability to prioritize and lead effective meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid technical foundation in electrical and mechanical systems, with a broad understanding of equipment systems (hardware, software, and process).&lt;/li&gt;
