&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The primary responsibility of this role is to manage and drive the process engineering function for a key product group in the ASM’s PECVD technology with a focus on results. This will require a strong leader that is highly skilled in people,&amp;nbsp;process&amp;nbsp;and technology across ASM’s PECVD operations. Further, the role requires someone who is not only skilled in R&amp;amp;D/Innovation, development,&amp;nbsp;engineering&amp;nbsp;and design for manufacturability, but also someone who is adept at process and organization, continuous improvement and working with and managing people across cultural dimensions in developing and delivering the PECVD technology roadmap. A persistent approach to Product Life Cycle (PLC) will be&amp;nbsp;required&amp;nbsp;to achieve strong engagement with the team,&amp;nbsp;develop&amp;nbsp;and implement new processes and organization, and manage the team to achieve PLC deliverables and drive projects to completion, exceeding&amp;nbsp;timelines&amp;nbsp;and budgetary&amp;nbsp;objectives. This position&amp;nbsp;facilitates&amp;nbsp;getting ASM products to market as quickly as possible by directly influencing and communicating with key customers to solve their high value problems. The successful candidate will have&amp;nbsp;a track record&amp;nbsp;of recruiting and&amp;nbsp;developing industry leading process engineering teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific&amp;nbsp;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the day-to-day management of the key product process engineering teams with an emphasis on results.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set, evangelize, and implement ASM processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embody ASM’s mission and&amp;nbsp;values, and&amp;nbsp;consistently reinforce them with the team through everyday actions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Product Lifecycle Cycle (PLC) team in developing and delivering next generation systems to the market.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for managing development execution (performance, cost, schedule, etc.).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support for existing products and drive continuous improvement efforts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work across organizations, particularly hardware and software engineering, to define success criteria of products and drive new product development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and&amp;nbsp;maintain&amp;nbsp;relationships with key customers. Work closely with the key account technology (KAT) organization to ensure that customer needs are met and qualification of new products and processes is done on time and to specifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to product roadmap by working with Product Marketing and key customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support&amp;nbsp;annual&amp;nbsp;strategic planning process to drive future business&amp;nbsp;direction.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully drive projects and recruit premier engineering talent.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Chemical Engineering, Material Science, Physics or Mechanical Engineering or related field,&amp;nbsp;required. Master or PhD preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience in semiconductor equipment development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record&amp;nbsp;of successfully building semiconductor equipment products under cost and ahead of schedule.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead and drive process engineering teams &amp;nbsp;through product development and market introduction with an ability to develop process engineering managers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record&amp;nbsp;of successfully managing, recruiting, developing, and scaling extraordinary teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive continuous improvement across operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business level English and Japanese&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
