&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Engineering (Electrical Engineering / Energy Engineering)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–10 years or more of experience in related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(Particularly within major construction companies and engineering groups.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holder of a Professional Engineer License in Electrical Engineer and Electrical Construction Engineer. (전기기사/ 전기공사기사 자경증 소지.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Cleanroom &amp;amp; utility system design and serving as a Site Representative (Construction Site Manager) for construction projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TOEIC score of 750 or above and the ability to communicate effectively in a business English environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TOEIC score of 800 or above and TOEFL iBT score of 90 or above.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience studying abroad for language training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead and influence across functions and organizational levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage construction projects independently with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer and results-oriented mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
