&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;ASM is an equal opportunity employer and considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, nationality, social or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender, gender identify or expression, marital status, pregnancy, political affiliation, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Job Description Summary&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ASM is seeking an EHS Engineer to help support a safe and sustainable workplace in the semiconductor equipment industry, primarily based at the Second Technology Center (TC2). In this role, you will work closely with the Senior EHS Manager to support EHS activities at the Tama and TC2 sites and help create an environment where employees, contractors, and visitors can work safely and confidently. You will also collaborate with Field EHS supporting domestic field service operations and provide EHS support to other sites in Japan as needed. Candidates with experience in manufacturing, facilities, field service, chemical safety, or occupational health and safety are encouraged to apply, even if they do not have direct semiconductor industry experience. Working with the Global EHS team and local stakeholders, you will contribute to practical, site-based EHS systems beyond compliance, including risk assessments, pre-installation and change reviews, chemical use reviews, tool installation reviews, training, audits, incident response, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Education / Experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience in engineering, science, chemistry, environmental health and safety, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience in EHS or occupational health and safety in manufacturing, semiconductor-related operations, equipment service, facility management, design, or development environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in semiconductor fabs, cleanrooms, or other high-tech manufacturing environments is preferred but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with chemical safety, hazardous materials, specialty gases, risk assessments, installation reviews, or incident response is preferred; experience with highly hazardous chemicals is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of ISO 14001, ISO 45001, Japanese environmental regulations, or occupational health and safety requirements is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills to collaborate effectively with diverse stakeholders, including operations teams, management functions, and global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage stakeholders across functions and levels and proactively contribute to improving the safety culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify issues based on site conditions and data, and propose and drive practical improvement actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn new knowledge, adapt to change, and grow independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work proactively, prioritize effectively, and remain flexible in a fast-changing business environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EHS-related qualifications such as Health Officer, Safety Officer, Occupational Safety Consultant, ISO auditor, or equivalent certifications are welcome but not required. Candidates who do not currently hold a Health Officer qualification are expected to obtain it after joining, with company support as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As an EHS Engineer at ASM, primarily based at TC2, you will support activities to improve safety and environmental performance at the Tama and TC2 sites while developing your EHS expertise through hands-on experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Senior EHS Manager to support and promote occupational health, safety, and environmental management activities at the Tama and TC2 sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Field EHS supporting domestic field service operations and provide support for EHS activities and site improvements at other locations as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compliance with applicable Japanese regulations, including the Industrial Safety and Health Act, Fire Service Act, and environmental laws, and contribute to stable business operations and risk reduction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If qualified, serve as the Health Officer for TC2 and support health and safety management activities required under Japanese regulations; if not already qualified, work toward obtaining the Health Officer qualification after joining.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide EHS guidance, site checks, and improvement support so that employees, contractors, and visitors can work safely and confidently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor changes in regulations, internal standards, and customer requirements, and provide practical recommendations to management and relevant functions based on EHS expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with operations and administrative teams to help resolve health and safety issues rooted in day-to-day site activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use EHS metrics, audit results, and incident information to drive improvement activities for risk reduction and stronger EHS performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain programs and procedures related to chemicals, hazardous materials, waste, and environmental management, and support proper implementation at each site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote the development and implementation of safe work plans, procedures, training, and management systems based on Japanese regulations, SEMI (Semiconductor Equipment and Materials International) standards, ASM Global procedures, and customer requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify potential risks early through risk assessments, work procedure reviews, and site checks, and link them to practical improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pre-introduction reviews for equipment, including Management of Change (MoC), to identify EHS risks associated with new equipment or changes and help develop necessary safety controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Chemical Approval Request reviews to evaluate risks, regulatory requirements, storage conditions, and handling requirements for chemicals, specialty gases, and hazardous materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support tool installation reviews, to verify EHS requirements, layout, utilities, work safety, and emergency response considerations before and after installation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous improvement of EHS performance through audits and site walkthroughs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with overseas sites and Global EHS members to deploy best practices across sites in Japan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate EHS issues, risks, and improvement proposals clearly, gaining stakeholder understanding and cooperation to move improvements forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the maintenance and improvement of emergency response plans for earthquakes, typhoons, fires, chemical leaks, and other potential emergencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to raising individual safety awareness and strengthening the safety culture through safety training and awareness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the event of an incident, help prevent recurrence and share lessons learned through initial response, root cause investigation, corrective and preventive action planning, and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge, Skills, Abilities - &lt;em&gt;We welcome candidates who can apply their EHS expertise to connect site operations with management and Japan activities with global initiatives, while proactively contributing to a safe and sustainable workplace.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic knowledge of semiconductor manufacturing equipment, cleanrooms, facilities, and chemical or gas handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust with internal and external stakeholders and communicate positively while staying close to site operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;English communication skills for emails, meetings, and document preparation with overseas members are preferred; TOEIC score of around 700 or equivalent English proficiency is a helpful guideline, not a strict requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to view change positively and respond flexibly in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify the root of issues and propose and drive practical improvements based on data and input from site teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to involve stakeholders across functions, build alignment, and lead improvement activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to adapt to a fast-changing environment where situations, direction, and strategy may evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in environments handling chemicals, hazardous materials, or specialty gases is preferred; candidates who are willing to learn and develop in this area are also welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in developing EHS expertise in a global environment and contributing to the safety culture of ASM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Officer qualification is preferred; candidates who do not already hold the qualification are expected to obtain it after joining. Other EHS-related qualifications such as Safety Officer, Licensed Hazardous Materials Handler, ISO 14001/ISO 45001-related qualification, or equivalent certification are also welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Travel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domestic and international travel may be required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;To learn more about ASM, find us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.asm.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;asm.com&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/asm/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ASMOfficialCompany&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/asmofficialcompany/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram,&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ASMofficialco&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/c/ASM_Official&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;ASM is an equal opportunity employer and considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, nationality, social or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender, gender identify or expression, marital status, pregnancy, political affiliation, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Specialist II, EHS you will report to the US Region EHS Lead and support the implementation and continuous improvement of Environmental, Health &amp;amp; Safety (EHS) programs for ASM&#39;s Service organization at an assigned site and associated customer locations. You will work closely with Field Service Engineers (FSEs), site leadership, customers, and EHS professionals to ensure service activities are conducted safely, compliantly, and in accordance with ASM requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role serves as the local EHS resource for service operations, helping to implement corporate and regional safety programs, support regulatory compliance, conduct field safety activities, facilitate training, investigate incidents, and drive continuous improvement. The position requires a strong field presence and regular interaction with employees and customers to promote a proactive safety culture.OSHA 511, ASP, CSP or other EHS certification preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Leadership Partnership &amp;amp; Safety Culture&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain strong working relationships with site leadership to support the integration of EHS expectations into daily service operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Service Managers and site leadership to identify safety risks, review performance trends, and develop practical risk reduction strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in site operational reviews, staff meetings, and leadership discussions to provide EHS guidance and support informed decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regularly communicate EHS performance, emerging risks, regulatory changes, and improvement opportunities to site leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support site leaders in fostering a positive safety culture through employee engagement, visible leadership activities, and proactive safety conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with site management to establish and track site-specific EHS objectives, action plans, and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching and consultation to supervisors and managers on EHS responsibilities, incident prevention, hazard recognition, and regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support leadership teams during incident investigations by identifying root causes, recommending corrective actions, and verifying implementation of improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate leadership participation in safety observations, Safety Management by Walking Around (SMBWA) activities, and site safety committee meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor to site leadership on EHS matters while promoting alignment with ASM policies, customer requirements, and industry best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Safety Program Implementation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement ASM EHS policies, standards, programs, and initiatives at assigned sites and customer locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support deployment of corporate and regional safety initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist local management in maintaining compliance with ASM EHS requirements and customer safety expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote safe work practices and support continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in implementation of safety, industrial hygiene, ergonomics, and risk reduction programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Regulatory and Customer Compliance&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain awareness of applicable regulatory requirements and customer EHS standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist employees and managers in understanding and complying with ASM and customer safety requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in customer safety meetings, audits, and assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compliance inspections and corrective action programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with maintaining site compliance documentation and records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Field Safety Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular field observations, safety walks, inspections, and behavioral safety engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach employees and contractors on hazard recognition and safe work practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a visible safety resource in customer facilities and ASM workplaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Safety Management by Walking Around (SMBWA) activities and safety observation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify hazards and recommend corrective actions to minimize operational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Incident Management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support reporting, investigation, and documentation of incidents, near misses, and occupational health concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in root cause investigations and corrective action development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track corrective actions to closure and verify effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support lessons learned communications and sharing across service teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Training and Awareness&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver safety training, toolbox talks, and EHS communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding and qualification activities for Field Service Engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain training records and verify completion of required safety training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce safety requirements through routine engagement with employees and managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Emergency Preparedness&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support maintenance of local emergency response plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in emergency drills and preparedness exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with customer emergency response personnel and local management as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Metrics, Audits, and Continuous Improvement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and analyze EHS performance data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal audits, customer assessments, and compliance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor corrective action completion and audit findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with identifying trends and opportunities to improve safety performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Education &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Occupational Health &amp;amp; Safety, Environmental Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, or related field preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience in occupational health and safety within manufacturing, semiconductor, high-technology, field service, facilities, or related industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of applicable occupational health and safety regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in semiconductor fabs, cleanroom environments, laboratories, or other high-tech manufacturing facilities preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting field service personnel, contractors, or customer-facing operations preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA 511, ASP, CSP or other EHS certification preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Knowledge, Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of occupational health and safety principles and practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of hazard recognition, risk assessment, and incident investigation methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with semiconductor manufacturing, equipment servicing, cleanroom environments, and customer facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with chemical, gas, industrial hygiene, ergonomic, and electrical safety hazards preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and follow-up capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence safe behaviors through collaboration and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while supporting broader organizational objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office and EHS data management tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Travel&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel between ASM facilities and customer facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other travel 10-25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Physical Demands&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The employee must be able to work within office, warehouse, laboratory, manufacturing, cleanroom, and customer environments. Responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standing and walking for extended periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accessing semiconductor fabrication facilities and working around semiconductor equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working around hazardous gases, chemicals, process equipment, and supporting facility infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wearing required personal protective equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work environment includes ASM offices, customer semiconductor manufacturing facilities, cleanrooms, warehouses, laboratories, and other operational environments where service personnel work. Compliance with customer and ASM EHS requirements is required at all times.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Success Profile&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A successful Senior Specialist I, EHS is highly visible in the field, technically knowledgeable, collaborative, customer-focused, and skilled at influencing safe behaviors. They translate ASM&#39;s EHS requirements into daily operational practices, helping ensure employees go home safely every day while supporting world-class service operations in the semiconductor industry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;To learn more about ASM, find us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.asm.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;asm.com&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/asm/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ASMOfficialCompany&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/asmofficialcompany/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram,&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ASMofficialco&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/c/ASM_Official&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;ASM is an equal opportunity employer and considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, nationality, social or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender, gender identify or expression, marital status, pregnancy, political affiliation, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

