&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Position Summary&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The EHS Engineer plays a critical role in advancing the company’s Environmental, Health, and Safety (EHS) objectives by ensuring compliance with applicable Japanese regulations, corporate policies, and industry standards. Leveraging technical expertise, this role drives the effective implementation and continuous improvement of the EHS management system to create a safe, healthy, and environmentally responsible workplace.&lt;br&gt;This position also supports site EHS leadership by translating global and regional strategies into actionable local initiatives and sustainable performance improvements. The EHS Engineer collaborates closely with cross-functional teams (e.g., manufacturing, facilities, and quality) to identify and mitigate risks, promote a proactive safety culture, and contribute to long-term EHS excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;CKM Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Project/Program Manager, Sales Director, Spare Team. Drive and forecast CKM, Spares and Part in supporting Micron F15.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support and coordinate CKM PM Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast and plan CKM Tool schedules and Revenue Projections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast Spare Parts and Coordinate with Logistics to expedite Orders from Customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Project/Program Manager, Sales Director, Spare Team and Finance on CKM Billings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Service Manager, Field Service/Process Engineers on Service Orders Quotations and Service Billings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Service Manager, Field Service/Process Engineers on SAP Purchase Requisitions and Procurements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competent in SAP, Search, Retrieve Part Number and Order. Retrieve Procedures, Draft RMA / FA and work with Customer on Service Report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform Failure Analysis on Defective Spare Parts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;POC to support and coordinate between cross functional teams for SAP HANA related matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;EHS Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the development, implementation, and maintenance of EHS policies and procedures in alignment with ISO 14001 and ISO 45001 standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compliance with local EHS regulations and company standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct basic risk assessments and hazard analyses to identify potential safety and environmental risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in incident investigations and support root cause analysis and corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and deliver EHS training sessions to employees and contractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Host monthly Safety Meeting to update Good catch and Incident situations in ASM/Micron and share them among Hiroshima team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support EHS audits and inspections and assist in addressing non-conformances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain emergency response plans and participate in emergency drills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor contractor activities to ensure compliance with EHS standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to environmental management initiatives including waste management and pollution control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the implementation of continuous improvement projects related to EHS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Administrative Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage general office administration tasks including scheduling, correspondence, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain office supplies and liaise with vendors for procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure proper filing and record-keeping of EHS and administrative documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a point of contact for internal and external stakeholders at the Hiroshima site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2-3 years of experience in EHS, order management or administrative roles, preferably in a manufacturing or industrial setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of using SAP application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and multitasking abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite and other administrative tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual (Japanese and English) communication skill&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
