&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deploy AIoT, computer vision, and intelligent automation solutions for manufacturing and operations.Integrate sensors, machine data, edge systems, vision systems, AI models, control environments, and enterprise applications while maintaining appropriate OT/IT segregation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead pilots for applications including machine monitoring, asset intelligence, assisted inspection, anomaly detection, and semi-autonomous workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate opportunities to use humanoid-assisted and intelligent automation for repetitive, constrained, hazardous, or ergonomically challenging tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define requirements, roadmaps, minimum viable product scope, success metrics, deployment plans, and adoption approaches using project and product management practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, operations, OT, IT, cybersecurity, vendors, and system integrators to address deployment architecture, integration readiness, commissioning, and sustainment needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish performance measures and support the transition from pilot to scaled operations, including ownership, training, support models, and value tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate technologies and vendors based on technical fit, cybersecurity risk, maintainability, scalability, supportability, and total cost of ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
