&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job&#39;s mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Test Engineer, you’ll play a critical role in turning breakthrough designs into real-world manufacturing solutions. From concept to customer delivery, you’ll drive new product industrialization by working cross-functionally to optimize for quality, cost, and lead time. You’ll be a strategic partner to both Global Operations and our Business Units, influencing design, improving processes, and supporting the full product lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop cost-effective testing methods with innovations on automation for systems and equipment testing throughout product development and manufacturing in meeting efficiency and customer quality requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide holistic technical solutions and drive standardization of testing methodology to produce consistent testing quality outcome in addressing testing needs across supplier, contract manufacturing, and internal manufacturing by liaising with cross functional teams in GOPS and Business Units (BU).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare test and diagnostic programs according to product requirements, refine detailed test specifications, develop detailed procedures, including assisting with the definition of test specifications with design / software engineering. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop hardware and software for test fixtures, plan and coordinate test fixture sourcing activities as needed, debug and deploy test fixtures for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gathers operational and test data to evaluate test results; may take corrective/continuous improvement actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with internal and external stakeholders to influence decisions and drive product testing improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in electrical/electronic engineering, automation engineering or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 8 years of experience in a manufacturing or engineering environment, ideally 5 years in semiconductor capital equipment industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in testing optimization, including test case/option addition, automation and standardization initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with control systems utilized in testing automation, serial communication protocols, TwinCAT PLC, DeviceNet, EtherCAT, RS 485, RS 232, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of testing methodology as well as programming languages such as C#, Python, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
