&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;nav-title&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot; href=&quot;../../sdash/4517589101&quot;&gt;Specialist I, Facility Management&lt;/a&gt; (Phoenix, AZ)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;At ASM, we are shaping the future of semiconductor manufacturing through innovation, collaboration, and excellence. We are seeking a Facility Specialist II to support our Phoenix operations by maintaining critical gas distribution systems, supporting semiconductor test operations, and ensuring safe, reliable facility performance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Working On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monitor and manage specialty gas distribution systems, including tracking gas usage and serving as a point of contact for Valve Manifold Box (VMB) operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perform gas cylinder change-outs and coordinate timely replenishment to support uninterrupted operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assist with gas system dry downs, final connections, disconnects, and commissioning activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support installation, startup, and qualification of gas distribution equipment and related infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Troubleshoot complex equipment and facility system issues, identifying root causes and implementing corrective actions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure compliance with all safety policies, procedures, and environmental requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support facility-related capital projects involving gas distribution systems and infrastructure upgrades.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assist in creating and maintaining operating procedures, work instructions, and system documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to support semiconductor manufacturing test operations and facility objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Participate in general facilities activities and support company events as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation providing 24/7 support for critical facility issues outside normal business hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;High school diploma or equivalent required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years of facilities, equipment, or related technical experience, preferably within the semiconductor industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience supporting gas distribution systems, gas cabinets, VMBs, or other semiconductor facility infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills with the ability to diagnose complex system and equipment issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent documentation, organizational, and time-management skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customer-focused mindset with strong communication and teamwork abilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working knowledge of semiconductor manufacturing processes and facility operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commitment to maintaining a safe work environment and following established safety procedures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to obtain Breathing Air (BA) Certification and successfully complete respirator fit testing requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Sets You Apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience supporting semiconductor cleanroom or laboratory environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of specialty gas systems, gas cabinets, VMBs, and associated safety requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience supporting facility capital projects, system installations, and equipment commissioning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to develop, improve, and document facility procedures and operating standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated ability to work independently, prioritize competing demands, and respond effectively in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong attention to detail and a proactive approach to identifying and resolving issues before they impact operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Passion for safety, continuous improvement, and operational excellence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why ASM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join ASM and help enable the technologies that power the future. You&#39;ll work alongside industry experts in a collaborative environment where innovation, learning, and career growth are encouraged. ASM offers competitive compensation, comprehensive benefits, and opportunities to make a meaningful impact in a global technology leader.&lt;/p&gt;
