&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job&#39;s mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an EHS Supervisor for ASM Taiwan, you will report to the Taiwan Site Services EHS Manager and join a global culture deeply committed to leading our industry in all aspects of EHS, Product Safety, and Sustainability. You will partner with customers and internal teams to ensure compliance with Taiwan regulations and ASM standards, driving continuous improvement in safety performance. This role offers opportunities to innovate and contribute locally and globally, while supporting semiconductor operations and projects. The position is responsible for the management of ASM EHS role in the southern part of Taiwan, including in the customers’ &amp;nbsp;facilities, supporting the customer service team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Requirement&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Up to 30%, primarily within Taiwan.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Environment : &lt;/strong&gt;Office and customer site environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all onsite operations comply with Taiwan legal requirements and ASM standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate EHS topics and training within projects and with customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct audits, risk assessments, accident investigations, and implement corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage high-risk work, contractor safety, and change management processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ISO45001/TOSHMS system implementation and audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver health and safety training programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with customers to integrate safety requirements into operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with government documentation and regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in EHS activities and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and analyze EHS metrics to the discovery of trends, and develop improvement plans to minimize risk and improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and maintain practices, procedures, training and management controls to ensure work is planned and conducted in a safe manner in accordance with national and local regulatory requirements, Semiconductor Equipment Manufacturing Industry (SEMI) standards, ASM global EHS procedures, and customer requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS in Industrial Safety/Health Engineering or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in EHS within semiconductor or electronics industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Level B Labor Safety and Health Management certification/license is mandatory&amp;nbsp;(乙級職業安全衛生管理員為必要條件).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge in the semiconductor equipment industry, including wafer processing equipment, servicing equipment, and ergonomics standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English (written and verbal).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of occupational safety and product safety principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What sets you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occupational health and safety experience in semiconductor fabs or other high-tech areas/semiconductor fabs preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with chemistry and materials technology is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence without authority and engage with a diverse range of employee and management levels within an organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured and detailed work approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-focused mindset with integrity and optimism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical skills with demonstrated problem solving ability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
